cpcbuild patch for Caprice32 (ColinPitrat/caprice32 8c778bf, GPLv2 like Caprice32).

Bug: Caprice32 keeps the Plus ASIC's DMA registers (&6C00-&6C0B address and
prescaler, &6C0F DCSR) in the ASIC register page buffer, but
asic_read_dcsr() and asic_update_dcsr() read and write them through
membank_write[], i.e. in whatever is mapped at &4000-&7FFF. With the ASIC
page out that is program RAM: every raster interrupt, DMA cycle and
interrupt acknowledge rewrites RAM at &6C00-&6C0F (DCSR and its mirrors).
This corrupted Starfall Plus's code at one memory layout.

Fix: those two functions use pbRegisterPage (the register page buffer)
instead. Behaviour with the page in is unchanged.

Apply from the Caprice32 root: git apply tools/caprice32/caprice32-asic-regs.patch

diff --git a/src/asic.cpp b/src/asic.cpp
index 9c1697d..623667e 100644
--- a/src/asic.cpp
+++ b/src/asic.cpp
@@ -111,8 +111,10 @@ static inline unsigned short decode_magnification(byte val) {
    return mag;
 }
 
+// DCSR and its mirrors live in the ASIC register page buffer, not in whatever
+// is mapped at &4000: with the page out that is RAM, which must not change.
 byte asic_read_dcsr() {
-  return *(membank_write[dcsr_addr >> 14] + (dcsr_addr & 0x3fff));
+  return pbRegisterPage[dcsr_addr & 0x3fff];
 }
 
 byte asic_compute_dcsr() {
@@ -140,7 +142,7 @@ void asic_update_dcsr(byte val) {
   // Writing the DCSR at all these addresses rather than handling this special
   // case on the read path allows for faster reads.
   for (auto addr = dcsr_addr & 0xfff0; addr <= dcsr_addr; addr++) {
-    *(membank_write[addr >> 14] + (addr & 0x3fff)) = val;
+    pbRegisterPage[addr & 0x3fff] = val;
   }
 }
 
